cc2ca1c8-f0d6-427a-b7cc-7753bc727569	6be7e2ff-0447-44a0-a3b5-64993b9db54d	2026-01-01	field_executive	4.35	4.35	needs_improvement	\N	\N	This is a new field sales executive whose initial performance indicates significant room for growth, particularly in core sales activities. While Collection Efficiency shows a positive start, nearly all other competencies are at 0% or very low, highlighting the need for foundational training and consistent execution.	[{"insight": "Your initial 80% collection rate is a commendable start, demonstrating a solid understanding or quick grasp of collecting payments on time. This is a crucial financial discipline.", "keepDoing": "Continue to prioritize timely collections and ensure all credit orders are tracked and followed up rigorously. Aim to maintain or improve this rate consistently.", "competency": "Collection Efficiency"}]	[{"timeline": "3 weeks", "competency": "Productivity & Visit Discipline", "targetScore": 70, "currentScore": 0, "specificActions": ["Complete a daily minimum of 5 productive visits, focusing on achieving the purpose of each visit.", "Ensure every visit is properly checked in and out using the system, including mandatory photo uploads for all visits.", "Review your sales route daily to optimize travel time and maximize the number of customer interactions."]}, {"timeline": "4 weeks", "competency": "Revenue Achievement & Territory Coverage", "targetScore": 50, "currentScore": 1.4, "specificActions": ["Work closely with your manager to understand your assigned territory and identify key accounts for immediate engagement.", "Set clear daily sales targets and focus on presenting key products during every customer interaction.", "Prioritize visits to retailers with the highest potential for sales growth, rather than just routine visits."]}]	{"weeklyFocus": {"week1": "Focus on understanding your territory and executing a minimum of 5 quality visits daily, concentrating on proper check-in/checkout and photo uploads for visit discipline.", "week2": "Continue executing daily visits, focusing on making them productive by identifying customer needs and presenting relevant products to generate initial revenue.", "week3": "Concentrate on increasing your revenue achievement by actively selling during visits and expanding product mix conversations. Practice overcoming sales objections.", "week4": "Review your progress across all competencies. Refine your visit planning and sales pitch based on feedback and initial results, aiming for consistent execution in productivity and sales."}, "motivationalNote": "Every great sales journey begins with a first step, and your strong start in collections shows your potential. Embrace these early challenges as opportunities to learn and grow. I'm confident that with focused effort and consistent execution, you will see significant improvement in your performance!"}	\N	f	\N	2026-01-13 05:15:40.624444+00	2026-01-13 10:18:15.181816+00	24f9138a-6390-44e6-901d-701d0d75702e
